  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 215 AM EDT Sat Oct 24 2026\n\nPatchy early morning fog potential will continue over the next \nseveral days, but mainly near rivers and lakes. \n\nWe remain in a persistent pattern of a large upper ridge centered to \nour west and surface high pressure extending into our area from the \nnorth and northeast. The ridge axis will shift gradually east, and \nshort wave energy moving through the Great Lakes Region will act to \ntemporarily suppress the ridge during the middle of next week. \nHowever, models continue to indicate we will remain dry for the \nentire period through next Friday.  \n\nFor the entire period we can expect seasonably cool nights and \npleasant afternoons with high temperatures generally a little above \nnormal for this time of year. We will also continue to see low \nrelative humidity values during the afternoon hours, but light winds \nwill help to mitigate notable fire weather concerns.",
